        "spokenScript": "One of the first things we did for a new venue client this summer was lower her ad budget.\n\nWhich, I know, is not what you'd expect to hear from an ads agency.\n\nBut when we asked her how she felt about her spend, she told us it had crept up over the year, her traffic was up, and her leads weren't any better. And she'd love to bring it down. So before we touched anything, we looked at what that money was actually doing.\n\nHer Google ads were working. But when a budget keeps climbing, Google can sometimes start assuming you're okay paying more for every lead. So we brought it down to about half and started fresh.\n\nOn Meta, the campaign that was spending the most hadn't brought in a single tracked lead. So we turned it off, right there on the call.\n\nAnd honestly, I loved that she asked. I think a lot of wedding pros feel like they're supposed to just keep spending more and hope it works out.\n\nThen we rebuilt everything at a lower budget, where every campaign has one clear job.\n\nBecause I'm all for investing in growth. I just want to know what's working before we put more behind it."
